<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05H6">Example <span data-tag="05H6">10.1.4.20</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $C_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. If the object $X = C_0$ admits a Čech nerve $\operatorname{\check{C}}_{\bullet }(X)$ (Definition <a data-tag="04SY" href="/tag/04SY">10.1.4.3</a>), then the identity map $C_0 \rightarrow X$ can be promoted to a morphism of simplicial objects $C_{\bullet } \rightarrow \operatorname{\check{C}}_{\bullet }(X)$ (see Notation <a data-tag="04SZ" href="/tag/04SZ">10.1.4.4</a>) which exhibits $\operatorname{\check{C}}_{\bullet }(X)$ as a $0$-coskeleton of $C_{\bullet }$. </p>
